Z||000000||Lurch||08-04-2001||05:59 PM||||Need info for getting proper vss signal to ecm.  88 coupe, Isuzu 5spd, 96 3100, 90 Lumina 7727 ecm.  According to the factory manual the ecm needs 24000 ppm signal, but fiero vss supplies 4000 ppm.  Called Dakota Digital about a signal converter but they don't sell one that will jack up the fiero signal that much.  Is there a vss that will fit the Isuzu that will furnish the proper signal to the ecm?  If so, can fiero speedo be driven by 4000 ppm IP signal from the ecm?  Members of the forum who have swapped later engines/ecms into manual trans cars maust have ran into this problem, but there doesn't seem to be a firm solution on the forum. Thanks for any info you may provide.||||reg||5
Z||000001||lowCG||08-04-2001||07:11 PM||||I was aware of that when I did my swap, the speedo is fine as the signal is sent to the ECM in a parallel wiring arrangement(same as stock,but with wires branching off to the ECM),and there hasn't been any problems as far as the ECM not getting an adequate signal.||||reg||1
